    <h1>Luvuyo Collen Mnguni</h1>
    <h2>AWS SysOps Engineer | IT Operations & Application Support Specialist</h2>

    <p class="tagline">
      AWS SysOps Engineer and IT Operations Specialist with hands-on expertise spanning cloud infrastructure,
      technical and application support, and IT service management (ITSM) in multinational environments.
    </p>

    <p class="contact">
      📍 Roodepoort, Gauteng |
      📧 mnguni.luvuyo@gmail.com |
      📞 068 289 8792 |
      🔗 linkedin.com/in/luvuyo-mnguni-80414438
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- SUMMARY -->
  <section id="summary" class="card">
    <h3>Professional Summary</h3>

    <p>
      AWS SysOps Engineer and IT Operations Specialist with hands-on expertise spanning cloud infrastructure,
      technical and application support, and IT service management (ITSM) in multinational environments.
      Reduced AWS non-production runtime by up to 99.8% and delivered approximately 40% in monthly cost savings
      through AWS Lambda and Amazon EventBridge automation, RDS scaling, and Auto Scaling Group (ASG) instance
      scheduling across 26 cloud environments.
    </p>

    <p>
      Provided Tier 1 to Tier 3 technical support and incident resolution under SLA pressure, backed by a strong
      ITIL foundation spanning Incident, Problem, and Change Management, Root Cause Analysis (RCA), escalation
      management, and service desk operations, with hands-on support experience across Salesforce CRM, Amazon
      Connect, AVAYA, and Remedy ITSM (BMC). Brings a decade of enterprise ERP and business-systems support
      (NICOR, MDA, SAP) and IT business analysis experience prior to specialising in cloud operations.
    </p>

    <p>
      Independently learned Grafana and built a CloudWatch-integrated monitoring dashboard from scratch, including
      IAM-based data source configuration and custom panel visualizations for key AWS infrastructure metrics.
      Developed a self-service ITSM portal that reduced repeat incidents and improved knowledge base quality
      across a 6-country operation.
    </p>

    <p>
      AWS Certified Cloud Practitioner (valid to September 2027); 13+ years of total progressive IT experience;
      currently completing a BSc Honours in Computing through UNISA, expected 2027.
    </p>
  </section>

